Closes https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/6832 https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/3438

Adds support for "Declared Errors" to tRPC, which adds to the existing errorFormatter with a factory API for custom error shapes which can be thrown from anywhere.

```ts
// Define application errors somewhere central
const BadPhoneError = createTRPCDeclaredError({
  code: 'UNAUTHORIZED',
  key: 'BAD_PHONE',
})
  .data<{
    reason: 'BAD_PHONE';
  }>()
  .create({
    constants: {
      reason: 'BAD_PHONE' as const,
    },
  });

export const appRouter = t.router({
  // Register errors to bypass the errorFormatter and propagate its shape to client, including in types
  registered: t.procedure.errors([BadPhoneError]).query(() => {
    throw new BadPhoneError();
  }),

  // Failing to register will result in a downgrade to an INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR which is passed through the global errorFormatter
  unregistered: t.procedure.query(() => {
    throw new BadPhoneError();
  }),
});

export type AppRouter = typeof appRouter;
```

Client usage is still a WIP but essentially boils down to a good type-discrimination story

```ts
// most basic case in a try-catch with vanilla client and so `error: unknown`
if (isTRPCClientError<AppRouter>(error)) {
  error.isDeclaredError('BAD_PHONE')
  error.isFormattedError()
}

// also new `safe` helpers for vanilla client and app-dir usage
const [result, error] = safe(trpc.path.query())
// error is now fully typed as a ClientError with any DeclaredErrors known to it
error.isFormattedError()
error.isDeclaredError('BAD_PHONE')

// and in tanstack integrations
const { data, error } = useQuery(trpc.path.queryOptions())
// error is equally safely typed as usage of safe() above
error.isFormattedError()
error.isDeclaredError('BAD_PHONE')
```

